Why ARMA?

ARMA combines both ideas.
-----------------------

AR Part
=======

Uses past prices.

Today's Price
↓
Yesterday's Price
↓
2 Days Ago Price

MA Part
=======

Uses past errors.

Today's Error
↓
Yesterday's Error
↓
2 Days Ago Error

Combined:

Past Prices
+
Past Errors
=========================

Real-Life Example
-----------------

Suppose Britannia share today is ₹4800.

MA Thinking
Yesterday forecast was wrong by ₹2.
Use that error to improve tomorrow's forecast.

AR Thinking
Yesterday price was ₹4795.
Use previous prices to estimate tomorrow.

ARMA Thinking
Yesterday price was ₹4795
AND
Yesterday forecast error was ₹2

Use both information sources.

This is why ARMA is usually better.

